WEBVTT

00:00:03.509 --> 00:00:09.109
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Tuesday the sixth. Are we all on? I can hear somebody's radio through Teams.</v>

00:00:10.789 --> 00:00:16.390
<v Grace Liu>Might be mine. Sorry. Did anyone see the football last night? Absolute nonsense, that last decision.</v>

00:00:18.679 --> 00:00:22.530
<v Callum Reid>I switched it off. Blood pressure's high enough coming in here.</v>

00:00:24.230 --> 00:00:29.829
<v Tomasz Nowak>You should've tried the traffic on the ring road. Twenty minutes looking at the same bumper.</v>

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:33.899
<v Sarah Okafor>You sound remarkably cheerful about it.</v>

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:43.390
<v Tomasz Nowak>Oh, lovely start. Then someone's new car in the car park taking up about a space and a half. Who's got the shiny blue one?</v>

00:00:45.460 --> 00:00:48.960
<v Priya Raman>Not me. Mine's the one held together by road dirt.</v>

00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:51.450
<v Callum Reid>Structural road dirt. Don't wash it.</v>

00:00:52.759 --> 00:00:57.310
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, before this becomes the motoring channel. What's already cleared from last night?</v>

00:00:58.689 --> 00:01:03.590
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah so, finished the repair on the line 3 chiller last night. That's done.</v>

00:01:04.019 --> 00:01:07.170
<v Callum Reid>Good. That was the one confusing the handover list.</v>

00:01:07.609 --> 00:01:14.260
<v Olumide Adeyemi>And I tested the line 2 yesterday and it's all fine now. Finished item, not another test for today.</v>

00:01:15.670 --> 00:01:17.420
<v Priya Raman>Yeah, understood. That one's closed.</v>

00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:24.519
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Also finished the repair on the outfeed conveyor last night. All three of those are completed.</v>

00:01:26.150 --> 00:01:29.299
<v Sarah Okafor>Lovely. Completed work, nothing new against any of those.</v>

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:35.230
<v Olumide Adeyemi>One observation, though. Heard a slight rattle from the line three, nothing to action yet.</v>

00:01:36.109 --> 00:01:39.609
<v Callum Reid>Right, just an observation. Not a repair being handed out.</v>

00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:48.439
<v Aisha Begum>Same sort of thing from me. Saw the pressure on the 11kV Switchboard dip for a few minutes, it came back on its own.</v>

00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:54.260
<v Priya Raman>Pressure on the 11kV Switchboard? That's the wording you've got?</v>

00:01:55.739 --> 00:02:04.840
<v Aisha Begum>Yeah, that's how it was described. I'm not calling it a diagnosed fault. It recovered on its own; just reporting what I saw, no action proposed.</v>

00:02:07.250 --> 00:02:10.400
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay. Keep that separate from the agreed jobs, then.</v>

00:02:12.439 --> 00:02:19.090
<v Grace Liu>And we're still waiting on parts for the dryer, nothing we can do until they arrive. That's still blocked.</v>

00:02:21.379 --> 00:02:26.280
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yep, the supplier still hasn't confirmed the delivery for the Compressed Air Dryer either.</v>

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:29.830
<v Callum Reid>So no change there, basically.</v>

00:02:30.379 --> 00:02:33.530
<v Grace Liu>No change. Nothing we can progress on that today.</v>

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:43.599
<v Sarah Okafor>One other bit of housekeeping: we were going to replace the belt on the big boiler but that's been pushed to next month so ignore it.</v>

00:02:44.289 --> 00:02:46.740
<v Tomasz Nowak>Right, off today's list. Fine by me.</v>

00:02:48.419 --> 00:02:54.020
<v Sarah Okafor>Actual work, then. We've got the risk assessment for work on the Waste Heat Boiler outstanding.</v>

00:02:55.800 --> 00:03:03.500
<v Aisha Begum>I'll update the risk assessment for work on the Waste Heat Boiler today. That's holding production up so it needs doing first.</v>

00:03:05.090 --> 00:03:09.639
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, absolutely. That's the production hold, so first means first on that one.</v>

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:15.189
<v Aisha Begum>Agreed. I'll do that before the other bits we've got here.</v>

00:03:16.280 --> 00:03:20.129
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Aisha Begum. Today, and first because it's holding production up.</v>

00:03:21.960 --> 00:03:27.909
<v Grace Liu>That's the distinction I wanted clear. The assessment is the outstanding bit, not a fresh maintenance job.</v>

00:03:28.389 --> 00:03:31.189
<v Aisha Begum>Exactly, yeah. Not widening it into anything else.</v>

00:03:33.469 --> 00:03:37.319
<v Sarah Okafor>And the shift handover report going round—where are we with that?</v>

00:03:39.620 --> 00:03:43.120
<v Aisha Begum>I'll send the shift handover report round tomorrow at 9:30.</v>

00:03:44.139 --> 00:03:48.340
<v Callum Reid>Tomorrow at 9:30, not this morning? Sorry, you clipped a bit there.</v>

00:03:49.340 --> 00:03:52.139
<v Aisha Begum>Tomorrow at 9:30, yeah. I'll send it then.</v>

00:03:53.729 --> 00:03:56.530
<v Sarah Okafor>Got it, Aisha Begum. Separate from today's assessment.</v>

00:03:58.909 --> 00:04:04.159
<v Grace Liu>Um, I'll organise the toolbox talk for the team this afternoon. No rush on that.</v>

00:04:06.590 --> 00:04:09.039
<v Sarah Okafor>Cheers, Grace. This afternoon, but no rush.</v>

00:04:11.479 --> 00:04:17.430
<v Grace Liu>Yep, I'll organise it this afternoon. It's not something that needs jumping ahead of the production hold.</v>

00:04:18.990 --> 00:04:23.189
<v Callum Reid>As long as the talk isn't a replay of last night's refereeing.</v>

00:04:24.490 --> 00:04:27.990
<v Grace Liu>Could do a whole session on poor decisions, couldn't we?</v>

00:04:28.360 --> 00:04:34.310
<v Priya Raman>Anyway—sorry, talking over you. I'll run the monthly fire alarm test at half two. That's fairly important.</v>

00:04:35.810 --> 00:04:39.660
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, Priya. Monthly fire alarm test at half two, fairly important.</v>

00:04:40.069 --> 00:04:41.819
<v Priya Raman>Yeah, I'll do it then.</v>

00:04:43.350 --> 00:04:47.550
<v Tomasz Nowak>Half two this afternoon, yeah? Not an alarm we're expecting this morning.</v>

00:04:47.939 --> 00:04:50.740
<v Priya Raman>Correct, half two this afternoon is the test.</v>

00:04:52.930 --> 00:04:58.879
<v Priya Raman>And I'll order spare parts for the Fire Alarm Panel by Wednesday. Normal priority on that one.</v>

00:05:00.170 --> 00:05:06.819
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Priya Raman. Spare parts for the Fire Alarm Panel by Wednesday, normal priority. Separate entry from the test.</v>

00:05:07.379 --> 00:05:11.579
<v Priya Raman>Yep, I'll get the order in by Wednesday. Normal priority, no escalation.</v>

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:16.089
<v Olumide Adeyemi>That's ordering spares, then, not saying there's another panel repair today?</v>

00:05:17.259 --> 00:05:20.060
<v Priya Raman>Exactly. Just the spare-parts order. No extra repair.</v>

00:05:21.930 --> 00:05:27.529
<v Sarah Okafor>And mine: I'll do a site visit at Kestrel in Leeds with the contractor next week.</v>

00:05:28.689 --> 00:05:33.240
<v Callum Reid>Right, Saz, that's you with the contractor at Kestrel in Leeds next week.</v>

00:05:34.740 --> 00:05:38.939
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep, I'll do that. Next week, not part of today's floor work.</v>

00:05:40.730 --> 00:05:44.230
<v Tomasz Nowak>Enjoy the roads. Apparently we've got enough traffic for everyone.</v>

00:05:45.699 --> 00:05:49.899
<v Sarah Okafor>Can't wait. Right, that's the agreed list, unless someone's heard something differently.</v>

00:05:51.480 --> 00:05:57.779
<v Callum Reid>No, clear from production. The Waste Heat Boiler risk assessment today is the one that needs doing first.</v>

00:05:59.069 --> 00:06:03.970
<v Aisha Begum>Yeah, I've got that first. Handover report tomorrow at 9:30, so those aren't competing.</v>

00:06:06.029 --> 00:06:11.629
<v Grace Liu>And the dryer stays blocked. Haven't quietly acquired a job on that while we've been talking.</v>

00:06:12.050 --> 00:06:16.250
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Same here. Completed repairs stay completed; the rattle was only an observation.</v>

00:06:17.850 --> 00:06:19.949
<v Sarah Okafor>Good. Nothing else added. Thanks, everyone.</v>
